KNOWNBUG
typename_associative_array1.sv

^\[main\.p0\] always \$typename\(main\.aa\) == "int\$\[int\]": PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p1\] always \$typename\(main\.aw\) == "int\$\[\*\]": PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p2\] always \$typename\(main\.as\) == "bit\[7:0\]\$\[string\]": PROVED .*$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
$typename gives "?" for associative arrays. The parser drops the index
type, so it is not available to $typename. Before #2301, the associative array
variables make the property check fail "unimplemented
boolbv_widtht::get_entry" first.
